---
display_code: "6.1"
title: Data and Information
paper: "1"
order: 10
---

Data and information covers how digital systems represent, store, and process
the raw material they operate on. This area underpins most of what follows in
Paper 1, from programming to database design to security.

Topics here progress from the smallest unit (a single value of a given type)
up to structured collections and the implications of how data is modelled.
